     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Going above 10 mg raises the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and it adds little extra blood pressure control.\n\nSome questions to check before I enter anything:\n- **Was 10 mg intended?** That is the usual maximum. Typical starting doses are 2.5\u20135 mg daily.\n- **Is this a deliberate high dose?** If so, please confirm it with your supervising resident or attending and pharmacy. I can then enter it with a note documenting that.\n- **Does the patient need more blood pressure control?** Adding a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor/ARB or a thiazide, is generally preferred to pushing amlodipine past 10 mg.\n\nTell me which dose you want, for example amlodipine 10 mg orally once daily, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
